IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-62. NOUNS of a numbered list, of a reference to a range of its paragraphs, and of a printed date pair. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Criminal Procedure (Enforcement Powers - Arrests) Law, 5756-1996. It records ONE reference: the words at the end of s 35(b), the paragraph that lists the offences
-- for which a person is a "security-offence suspect" in that Law, which cite "paragraphs (1) to (5)" of the list, and what each paragraph of the list is (paragraph (5) is printed as deleted).
-- A range that names a paragraph printed as deleted is kept in an expected-red file; the sound paragraphs are the control.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the list.
-- The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module (`src:` lines are the Law's consolidation, `ext:[SH ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument).

§ `Nouns of a reference to a range of paragraphs`

-- Three kinds of reading, from the strongest to the weakest this row has.
-- The second kind is the honest name for the readings of the instruments here: the official page was read, but that no LATER instrument touched the words rests on the consolidation alone.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A paragraph of the list` HAS
    `its number` IS A NUMBER
    `the consolidation prints text for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consolidation prints it as deleted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instrument that adds it` IS A STRING
    `the instrument that directs its deletion` IS A STRING
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

DECLARE `A range reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the first paragraph named` IS A NUMBER
    `the last paragraph named` IS A NUMBER
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a printed date pair`

-- A Hebrew date and a Gregorian date printed together. The Hebrew date is written in Latin letters here, so that this file holds no Hebrew that its source does not hold; the Hebrew is on the `ext:` lines.
-- The third field is what the Hebrew-calendar routine in tools/hebcal.py gives for the Hebrew date; the routine is not part of this module.
DECLARE `A printed date pair` HAS
    `the Hebrew date, transliterated` IS A STRING
    `the Gregorian date printed with it` IS A DATE
    `the Gregorian date the calendar routine gives` IS A DATE
    `the pair was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
